E-Commerce API

A modern and scalable RESTful API for an e-commerce platform. This API provides essential features such as customer registration, authentication, product management, category management, and product search.

Features

Customer registration

Customer authentication (login)

Product creation

Product search

Category creation

Get category by ID

RESTful architecture

JSON-based responses

Tech Stack

Node.js

Express.js

MySQL (or any SQL database)

JWT (for authentication)

Base URL
http://localhost:3000/api

Authentication

Some routes (like product creation and category creation) may require authentication using JWT.

Include the token in the Authorization header:

Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN

API Routes
1. Customer Registration

Register a new customer in the system.

Endpoint:

POST /customers/register


Request Body:

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "123456"
}


Response:

{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Customer registered successfully"
}

2. Customer Login

Authenticate a customer and receive a JWT token.

Endpoint:

POST /customers/login


Request Body:

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "123456"
}


Response:

{
  "success": true,
  "token": "jwt_token_here"
}

3. Create Product

Create a new product in the store.

Endpoint:

POST /products


Headers:

Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json


Request Body:

{
  "name": "Running Shoes",
  "description": "Comfortable running shoes",
  "price": 199.99,
  "categoryId": 1,
  "stock": 10
}


Response:

{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Product created successfully"
}

4. Search Products

Search products by name, keyword, or filters.

Endpoint:

GET /products/search?q=keyword


Query Parameters:

q (string) – Search keyword

Example:

GET /products/search?q=shoes


Response:

{
  "success": true,
  "products": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "name": "Running Shoes",
      "price": 199.99
    }
  ]
}

5. Get Category by ID

Retrieve a specific category using its ID.

Endpoint:

GET /categories/:id


Example:

GET /categories/1


Response:

{
  "success": true,
  "category": {
    "id": 1,
    "name": "Sneakers"
  }
}

6. Create Category

Create a new product category.

Endpoint:

POST /categories


Headers:

Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json


Request Body:

{
  "name": "Sneakers"
}


Response:

{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Category created successfully"
}

Project Structure (Example)
src/
├── controllers/
├── services/
├── repositories/
├── routes/
├── middlewares/
└── app.js

Installation

Clone the repository:

git clone https://github.com/your-username/ecommerce-api.git


Install dependencies:

npm install


Configure environment variables:
Create a .env file:

PORT=3000
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_USER=root
DB_PASSWORD=your_password
DB_NAME=ecommerce
JWT_SECRET=your_secret_key


Run the project:

npm run dev

Error Handling

All errors follow a standard response format:

{
  "success": false,
  "error": "Error message"
}
